        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 113.75999999999999,
          "end": 116.78999999999999,
          "en": "that contains all our other widgets in the end.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 116.78999999999999,
          "end": 120.03,
          "en": "This material app widget is the widget you use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 120.03,
          "end": 122.343,
          "en": "for setting up your app's theme.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.24,
          "end": 126.81,
          "en": "Because I mentioned before that this app widget does a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 126.81,
          "end": 128.49,
          "en": "of behind the things stuff,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 128.49,
          "end": 132.6,
          "en": "but it also gives you some key configuration settings",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 132.6,
          "end": 136.02,
          "en": "that you can make here that influence your entire app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 136.02,
          "end": 139.02,
          "en": "And the theme is one of those settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 139.02,
          "end": 141.18,
          "en": "And indeed, at this point here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 141.18,
          "end": 143.52,
          "en": "I already have a theme set up.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 143.52,
          "end": 147.32999999999998,
          "en": "I got theme data set to use material three to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 147.32999999999998,
          "end": 151.65,
          "en": "that my app here uses this material three look.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 151.65,
          "end": 154.32,
          "en": "Now, this might not be necessary anymore at the point",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 154.32,
          "end": 155.85,
          "en": "of time you are viewing this video",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 155.85,
          "end": 158.88,
          "en": "because material three might be the default by then,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 158.88,
          "end": 160.62,
          "en": "but this theme parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 160.62,
          "end": 163.59,
          "en": "that can be set on this material app will be useful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 163.59,
          "end": 167.28,
          "en": "nonetheless, because setting up a theme is not just about",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 167.28,
          "end": 171.84,
          "en": "switching between the material three or material two looks,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 171.84,
          "end": 174.564,
          "en": "but instead you can use this theming mechanism",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 174.564,
          "end": 179.01,
          "en": "to control in detail which color different widgets in your",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.01,
          "end": 180.21,
          "en": "app will have,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 180.21,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "and which colors you want to be able to use in your app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 187.293,
          "en": "and which text styles you want to be able to use and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 188.4,
          "end": 192.09,
          "en": "So how can you then customize this theme?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 192.09,
          "end": 196.44,
          "en": "Customizing your applications theme involves setting this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 196.44,
          "end": 199.26,
          "en": "theme parameter here on the material app",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 199.26,
          "end": 200.85,
          "en": "as we're already doing it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 200.85,
          "end": 205.71,
          "en": "And theme wants a theme data object, which can be created",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 205.71,
          "end": 209.403,
          "en": "with this theme data class provided by Flutter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 210.39,
          "end": 213.57,
          "en": "Now, when instantiating this theme data class,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 213.57,
          "end": 215.716,
          "en": "you get many parameters that you can set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 215.716,
          "end": 218.82,
          "en": "to fine tune your app's theme.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 218.82,
          "end": 221.04,
          "en": "And this can be super overwhelming.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 221.04,
          "end": 222.3,
          "en": "And I will also say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 222.3,
          "end": 225.12,
          "en": "that Flutter's theming system,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 225.12,
          "end": 228.3,
          "en": "whilst being quite powerful and flexible,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 228.3,
          "end": 230.94,
          "en": "also evolved a lot over time",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 230.94,
          "end": 235.59,
          "en": "and therefore this theme data class here also allows you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 235.59,
          "end": 239.07,
          "en": "to set a lot of parameters which still work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 239.07,
          "end": 241.11,
          "en": "but shouldn't be used anymore",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 241.11,
          "end": 243.66,
          "en": "because they might be removed in the future",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 243.66,
          "end": 247.38,
          "en": "and there are better ways of configuring your theme.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 247.38,
          "end": 249.36,
          "en": "It's also worth pointing out",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 249.36,
          "end": 253.47,
          "en": "that if you create a theme data object like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 253.47,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "by instantiating theme data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 257.88,
          "en": "and then passing some configuration",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 257.88,
          "end": 261.57,
          "en": "between those parentheses, you are actually telling Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 261.57,
          "end": 265.05,
          "en": "that you are setting up the entire theme from scratch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 265.05,
          "end": 269.13,
          "en": "which means that theoretically you really should configure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 269.13,
          "end": 272.58,
          "en": "all these aspects that make up your application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 272.58,
          "end": 276.42,
          "en": "You should configure all text styles you could possibly use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 276.42,
          "end": 279.3,
          "en": "You should configure all other styles that might be used",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 279.3,
          "end": 281.25,
          "en": "by any widgets in your app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 281.25,
          "end": 285.48,
          "en": "And whilst this of course can make sense for certain apps,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 285.48,
          "end": 287.31,
          "en": "it also means a lot of extra work",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 287.31,
          "end": 291.3,
          "en": "because you might be happy with some default theme styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 291.3,
          "end": 293.82,
          "en": "that Flutter applies otherwise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 293.82,
          "end": 296.07,
          "en": "Now of course, you could argue that this app here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 296.07,
          "end": 300.15,
          "en": "by default doesn't look that horrible, and that is correct,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 300.15,
          "end": 303.33,
          "en": "but you'll see a difference if I switch to a different way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 303.33,
          "end": 306.27,
          "en": "of setting up my theme - a way which I would actually",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 306.27,
          "end": 309.78,
          "en": "recommend using. Instead of creating your theme data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 309.78,
          "end": 310.86,
          "en": "like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 310.86,
          "end": 313.53,
          "en": "It's better if you don't pass anything",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 313.53,
          "end": 315.12,
          "en": "to this constructor here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 315.12,
          "end": 318.42,
          "en": "and you instead call copy with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 318.42,
          "end": 321.93,
          "en": "and then to copy with you pass your settings.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 321.93,
          "end": 325.653,
          "en": "Like for example, in my case here, use material three true.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 326.58,
          "end": 327.9,
          "en": "If you do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 327.9,
          "end": 331.11,
          "en": "and you force a reload, at least for me, I always have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 331.11,
          "end": 332.19,
          "en": "to force a reload",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 332.19,
          "end": 334.83,
          "en": "to make these theme settings have an effect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 334.83,
          "end": 336.42,
          "en": "on the running app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 336.42,
          "end": 337.8,
          "en": "If you do that, you will see",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 337.8,
          "end": 340.47,
          "en": "that it now looks slightly different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 340.47,
          "end": 341.85,
          "en": "It looks slightly different.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 341.85,
          "end": 345.15,
          "en": "For example, this text in the title here looks different,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 345.15,
          "end": 348.03,
          "en": "and I would argue looks a bit better",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 348.03,
          "end": 352.47,
          "en": "because now we're actually preserving some better default",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 352.47,
          "end": 355.71,
          "en": "styles that are applied by default, by Flutter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 355.71,
          "end": 359.01,
          "en": "and we can now override selected styles with",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 359.01,
          "end": 361.14,
          "en": "that copy with method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 361.14,
          "end": 364.26,
          "en": "So instead of setting up an entire theme from scratch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 364.26,
          "end": 366.96,
          "en": "and having to style everything from scratch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 366.96,
          "end": 370.41,
          "en": "we're now using some default themes set up by Flutter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 370.41,
          "end": 373.41,
          "en": "and we're only overriding selected styles",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 373.41,
          "end": 377.4,
          "en": "or selected aspects of that theme, you could say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 377.4,
          "end": 381,
          "en": "For example, we could now also target another parameter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 381,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "here in this copy with method, which we're calling,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 388.38,
          "en": "and set the scaffold background color to any color",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 388.38,
          "end": 391.92,
          "en": "of our choice, and maybe not red, I'll just use this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 391.92,
          "end": 394.11,
          "en": "as a starting point to pick a color.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 394.11,
